From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 23:29:50 -0400
Subject: settings: manage the window's Spaces from chrome://settings

A "Spaces" list in the Stedding section shows this window's Spaces with
their swatch and icon. Typing a new name renames the Space (the switcher
follows at once), the bin deletes one and is disabled for the last, and the
list refreshes whenever the sidebar adds, renames or removes a Space. A
SettingsPageUIHandler finds the window that hosts the settings tab, observes
its SpaceModel and pushes the list.

Why: docs/features/settings.md T9; the sidebar's context menu is the only
other place a Space can be renamed or deleted, and settings is where users
look for it.

Removable when: never; this is product behaviour.
